# ---- Per-mod content -------------------------------------------------------
# A mod directory ships its TOOLS; the content they build is regenerated.  A .unit
# carries a native template's trailer spliced into it, a .level is a donor level with
# only its entity table replaced, and a .glb is the authoring input - all game-derived
# and rebuilt by one command.  Nothing of that kind has ever been published here: no
# .level, .unit, .glb or mod.json is tracked, and a mod definition describes files that
# exist only after a build.  So keep the *.py files in these directories (deliberately
# NOT matched below) and ignore everything else.
scripts/plane_mod/*
!scripts/plane_mod/*.py
scripts/level_probe_mod/

# ---- Bundle build scratch -------------------------------------------------
# A bundle belongs in the loader's mods/bundles/<Name>/.  These are the same file set
# built with scripts/ as the working directory; the body is 116 KB of game-derived
# resources and every build rewrites it.
scripts/5aa67cb8548c3281
scripts/bundle.ini
scripts/manifest.json

# ---- Scratch -------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp.*
.DS_Store

# Video-mining scratch (captions, OCR dumps, downloads, venv)
Stingray-Video-Mine/

Stingray_Documentation/

# Web-mining scratch (article markdown, downloaded screenshots, OCR dumps)
Stingray-Web-Mine/

# Big-run scratch (mutate seeds/tokens/logs - regenerated constantly)
hashcracker/work/

# transfer bundles (tools/make_transfer_bundle.sh)
hashcracker-state-*.tar.gz

# current game install, copied in for a self-contained transfer archive
# (do NOT commit: ~1.5 GB of shipped game data)
Gauntlet-install/

# Shell drivers are LOCAL-ONLY: they carry machine/host specifics and are never
# published (see .clinerules - "personal data in a tool must never be pushed").
# The Python tools + their data are the repo; the .sh plumbing runs on the machine.
*.sh

# ---- Local-only (machine/personal; never published) ----------------------
.clinerules
.githooks/
ARCHIVE-CONTENTS.md
hashcracker/TRANSFER.md
hashcracker/REMOTE-GPU.md

# ---- Game-derived, local-only (kept on disk, never pushed) ---------------
# the shipped Lua source tree, copied in for mining; not redistributed
game-source/
# locally-cached liveness probe results
scripts/.liveness_cache/
# level_from_glb.py's kind -> material table: a cache, not authored data - the tool
# rebuilds it by rescanning the shipped levels whenever the file is missing
Data/kind_materials.json
# reference images extracted from the Stingray docs
Data/Stingray_Documentation/
